  "irVersion": 8,
  "notes": {
    "mutation-judge": "Decides whether a mutation report passes the mutation gate, value by value and as a whole.",
    "mutation-judge.does.begin": "A decision-table value is judged next: whether it is a number, and whether it appears in the adapter as a number. None of its sites has been given yet.",
    "mutation-judge.does.end": "The value's sites are over. If it had a site, a value is located in production code (for the rest of the judgement), and if none of its sites was killed, it survived. If it had no site, and it is a number that appears in the adapter, it is in the adapter.",
    "mutation-judge.does.finish": "The judgement is over. If no value was located in production code, no mutant was killed, and the production code is not shared with other components in a way that could not be narrowed (shared), the mutation is ineffective.",
    "mutation-judge.does.mutant": "A mutant (every one, the sites of values included) and whether it was killed.",
    "mutation-judge.does.site": "A site of the value: a place in production code where the value was changed, and whether that made the tests fail (killed).",
    "mutation-judge.state.anyKilled": "Whether some mutant so far was killed.",
    "mutation-judge.state.located": "Whether some value so far had a site.",
    "mutation-judge.state.sawSite": "Whether the value being judged has a site (a place in production code where it was broken).",
    "mutation-judge.state.siteKilled": "Whether some site of the value being judged was killed (breaking it made the tests fail).",
    "mutation-judge.state.valueInAdapter": "Whether the value being judged is a number that appears in the adapter.",
    "verdict": "What the judgement reports."
  },
